1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,520
Chick-fil-A makes more than these three businesses combined.

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,980
So here are the six things they do

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,120
that you can apply to your business.

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,320
Number one is focus.

5
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,240
They focused on selling chicken sandwiches

6
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,320
for the past 59 years in making the chicken sandwich

7
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,280
better and better and better.

8
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:14,880
Number two, they built slowly.

9
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,440
Chick-fil-A grew slowly, didn't take on debt as family owned.

10
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:19,700
It's competitor in the early days Boston market

11
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,240
who as fast as they could took on debt

12
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,920
when public announced out of business.

13
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,160
Number three, values.

14
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,920
Chick-fil-A could increase their sales by 13%,

15
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:31,920
or $650 million per year by simply being open on Sunday.

16
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:34,040
But they don't let money compromise their values

17
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,520
which makes them more money in the long term.

18
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,920
Number four, hospitality.

19
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,400
They hired people from Ritz Carlton

20
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,680
to help them create exquisite experiences at Chick-fil-A.

21
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,920
Number five, compounding.

22
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,680
They buy the land and the building

23
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,480
for each door they build

24
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,000
so over time the real estate value continues

25
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:46,880
to go up and compound.

26
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,760
Number six, they don't change their menu.

27
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:49,600
And this is huge.

28
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,280
They just get better and better at what they sell.

29
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,200
So instead of being mediocre at many things,

30
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,400
they're exceptional at a few.

31
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:57,000
Their menu is a quarter of the size

32
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,320
of many other big faster chains

33
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:00,960
and all the stuff down there is arguably, in my opinion, better.

34
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,360
Tactics like these help me build my portfolio of companies

35
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,200
that generate over $250 million annually.

